# Line endings are part of the binary: rules/default.toml and
# rules/contacts.toml are compiled into witness.exe with include_str!.
# A checkout that converts them to CRLF (git's default on Windows) builds a
# binary 300 bytes larger than one that keeps LF, and the release hash no
# longer reproduces. Observed 2026-09-30: GitHub's runner vs the maintainer's
# machine, identical toolchains, 512 bytes apart, CRLF the only difference.
# So every text file is LF in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
* text=auto eol=lf
